From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram_netlist -periphery unplaced
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-periphery unplaced leaves the periphery (address inverters and
registers, decoders, select buffers, each word's select cell and the
input buffers) for a parent to place, size and buffer: the parent alone
knows the drivers and loads outside the array. The outline is cut to
what stays placed, the core, and a row above it for a parent of the
other row parity, so a parent sizing its floorplan by utilization
charges the core and nothing else. Each pin goes where its connections
land, on -pin_layer's track grid inside the outline, for a macro
placer to orient the core by before the parent dissolves it into its
own rows. generate_ram_netlist only; generate_ram's flow places
everything.

Tested: src/ram/test/periphery_unplaced_asap7.tcl.

Commit 9 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
